Package: relweights
Type: Package
Title: Relative Weight Analysis for Linear Models and Structural Equation Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("George", "Michaelides", email = "g.michaelides@uea.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Relative weight analysis (Johnson, 2000,
    <doi:10.1207/S15327906MBR3501_1>) divides the explained variance
    (R-squared) of a regression among correlated predictors. The analysis
    works directly on fitted linear models from stats::lm() and on structural
    equation models fitted with 'lavaan'. For 'lavaan' models, the weights of
    every structural regression, including regressions among latent
    variables, are computed from the model-implied correlation matrix,
    separately for each group and level. Results report raw and rescaled
    weights together with standardized coefficients, the coefficients of the
    orthogonal counterparts and zero-order correlations. Bootstrap percentile
    confidence intervals and 'ggplot2' visualisations are available.
